  "worked_solution": "A similarity transformation is any transformation made up of rigid motions (rotations, reflections, and translations) and dilations. \n\nA similarity transformation will map any polygon to a similar polygon.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the transformations in turn.\n\n- Transformation I represents a stretch of factor $2$ in the $x$-direction and a stretch of factor $4$ in the $y$-direction. This is not a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation II represents a dilation of scale factor $3$ and center $O.$ Thus, it is a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation III represents a reflection in the $x$-axis. Thus, it is a rigid motion and, therefore, a similarity transformation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
